course: dictionary
lesson: 15897
title: Unlawful and the law
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: The word «unlawful» is made of two parts: un- means not, and lawful means allowed by the law. So unlawful means not allowed by law, or against the law. Another word for it is illegal.
explain: «It is unlawful to park on a yellow line.» A law is a rule that a whole country agrees to follow. If something is unlawful, it breaks that rule. The rule is there to keep people safe or fair.
explain: Unlawful is a formal word. You will meet it in news reports and in lessons about the law. «The shop was fined for selling fireworks unlawfully.» Here unlawfully is the adverb: it tells you how the shop acted, which was against the law.
explain: Be careful: unlawful is not the same as rude or unkind. «Shouting at a friend is unkind, but it is not unlawful.» Something can be bad manners and still be allowed by law. Ask yourself: does the law say no?
fact: Unlawful means not allowed by law, or against the law.
fact: «Unlawful» means the same as illegal.
fact: The prefix un- means not, as in unkind, unfair and unlawful.
fact: «Unlawfully» is the adverb: «He entered the building unlawfully» means he went in against the law.
fact: Being rude or unkind is not always unlawful; the word only fits actions that break the law.
exercise: «Taking money from someone's bag without asking is unlawful.» What does unlawful mean? | Full of bright colours | Loud and noisy | Very kind and helpful | *Against the law
exercise: Mia says unlawful means the same as illegal. Is she right? | Only in football matches | No, illegal means very sick | *Yes, both words mean against the law | No, they mean opposite things, so unlawful means allowed
exercise: «Dropping litter is untidy, but it is not always unlawful.» Find and copy the word that means not allowed by law. | untidy | litter | always | *unlawful
test: «Sam was told that sneaking into the cinema without paying was unlawful.» What does unlawful mean in this sentence? | Not allowed by law | *Against the law, like breaking a rule that the country has made | Very expensive | Funny and silly
test: «He entered the bank unlawfully.» What does unlawfully mean here? | In a quiet and gentle way | In a hurry to catch a bus | *In a way that is against the law | With a smile on his face
exam: «The judge said the driver's unlawful action put other people in danger.» Which word tells you that the driver broke the law? | *unlawful | dangerous | judge | people
